  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "A red box contains three red marbles and one blue marble. A blue box contains two blue marbles and one red marble. An experiment is performed 100 times: draw a marble from a box, note its colour, and replace it. The first draw is from the red box. Each subsequent box is chosen by the colour of the last marble: if red, draw next from the red box; if blue, from the blue box. Find the probability that:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the first marble is red",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac34$",
          "worked": "$$P(R_1)=\\frac34.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the first marble is blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac14$",
          "worked": "$$P(B_1)=\\frac14.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "the second marble is red",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{31}{48}$",
          "worked": "Add the probabilities of the paths $RR$ and $BR$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(R_2)&=\\frac34\\times\\frac34+\\frac14\\times\\frac13\\\\P(R_2)&=\\frac9{16}+\\frac1{12}\\\\P(R_2)&=\\frac{31}{48}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "the second marble is blue",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{17}{48}$",
          "worked": "Add the probabilities of the paths $RB$ and $BB$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B_2)&=\\frac34\\times\\frac14+\\frac14\\times\\frac23\\\\P(B_2)&=\\frac3{16}+\\frac16\\\\P(B_2)&=\\frac{17}{48}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "the third marble is red",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{347}{576}$",
          "worked": "The second marble determines the box used for the third draw.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(R_3)&=P(R_2)\\times\\frac34+P(B_2)\\times\\frac13\\\\P(R_3)&=\\frac{31}{48}\\times\\frac34+\\frac{17}{48}\\times\\frac13\\\\P(R_3)&=\\frac{279}{576}+\\frac{68}{576}\\\\P(R_3)&=\\frac{347}{576}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "the third marble is blue.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{229}{576}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(B_3)&=P(R_2)\\times\\frac14+P(B_2)\\times\\frac23\\\\P(B_3)&=\\frac{31}{48}\\times\\frac14+\\frac{17}{48}\\times\\frac23\\\\P(B_3)&=\\frac{93}{576}+\\frac{136}{576}\\\\P(B_3)&=\\frac{229}{576}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q8-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
